   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Some results are in the Initial Environmental Examination | Apr 2023: https://www.adb.org/sites/default/files/project-documents/53264/53264-001-iee-en_0.pdf</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: GAP training modules for all crops, with 14 GAP training modules have been finalized. 85 GAP trainings have been completed on Pomegranate, Orange, Strawberry, Okra, Chili, Custard Apple, Banana, flowers, Strawberry, Guava, Mango, Cashew, Sapota and lemon; a total of 16,677 farmers including 4,288 women (25.71%) participated.

Business Development Plans (BDPs) of 62 FPOs have been prepared by TA consultant. Total 11 Buyers procured total 270 MTs of fruits and vegetables amounting Rs. 1.06 Cr from 12 different sellers i.e. (10 FPOs &amp; 2 VCOs).

47 matching grant subprojects sanctioned (31 FPOs and 16 VCOs). Out of 47 subprojects 10 are owned or led by women). 2 proposals cancelled due non-start of activities. Total grant sanctioned to 47 subprojects INR 124.66 crore of which INR 16.06 crore for these 10 women owned/led subproject. (12.88 % of sanctioned grant amount)

3 Financial Intermediaries (i) Samunnati Financial Intermediation and Services Private Ltd, (ii) Bank of India, and (iii) The Federal Bank have signed financing agreements with MAGNET Society for extending financial intermediary loans to FPOs and VCOs. Samunnati has extended finance to 41 beneficiaries amounting to INR 30 crore.

Construction activities initiated at 18 project locations. Gender-responsive features identified. Out of 18 sites 6 sites have been completed.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
